 RESONANCE REGION                                                 6925 1451
 Authors: G.P.A. Nobre, S.F. Mughabghab, A. Palumbo, M. Herman    6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
  RESOLVED RESONANCES in MLBW                                     6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
   S-wave resonance parameters below 1945 eV were adopted from    6925 1451
   the Atlas of Neutron Resonances[Mu06]                          6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
   A bound level was invoked to reproduce 2200 m/s capture cross  6925 1451
     section of 105 b and a bound coherent scattering length of   6925 1451
     7.07 fm [Mu06].                                              6925 1451
   Effective scattering radius of 7.7 fm was adopted from         6925 1451
     from the Atlas [Mu06].                                       6925 1451
     section in the unresolved energy region.                     6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
   L values that had not been determined from measurements were   6925 1451
      assigned by applying the Bayesian approach.                 6925 1451
   J values which were not determined from measurements were      6925 1451
     assigned randomly to follow the 2J+1 rule                    6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
  Calculated thermal cross sections & resonance integrals:        6925 1451
      ---------------------------------------------               6925 1451
      Reaction       Cross section    Res. integral               6925 1451
                        (barn)           (barn)                   6925 1451
      Total           111.96                -                     6925 1451
      Elastic           6.95                -                     6925 1451
      Capture         105.00             1624.5                   6925 1451
      ---------------------------------------------               6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
     With these parameters, the Wescott factor for the capture    6925 1451
     reaction is calculated as g_w = 1.00870 .                    6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
  UNRESOLVED RESONANCE REGION in 'all energy-dependent parameters'6925 1451
                              format (LRF=2)                      6925 1451
  Author S.F. Mughabghab                                          6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
     The Unresolved energy region covers neutron energies         6925 1451
   from 1.94 kev to the the first inelastic channel at 8.46 keV.  6925 1451
   Strength function for s-wave neutrons, S0= 2.22,               6925 1451
   and  average radiative widths for s- and p-wave neutrons,121.9 6925 1451
   meV and 61.0  meV respectively, which were derived             6925 1451
   in the unresolved energy region are adopted from               6925 1451
   the work of Mughabghab [Mu10,Mu11].For d-wave neutrons the     6925 1451
   average capture width,96.4 meV, is obtained as the geometric   6925 1451
   mean of the s- and p-wave components[Mu10] .                   6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
   Note that S0 = 2.22, as well as the average capture width      6925 1451
   for s-wave neutrons, 121.9-+2.6 meV,in the URR differ          6925 1451
   significantly from those derived in the resolved resonance     6925 1451
   region below 2.6 keV (S0 = 1.6-+0.12, GG0=86-+7 meV, Atlas     6925 1451
   recommendation). The difference can be attributed to the       6925 1451
   possible presence of a doorway state above neutron energy of   6925 1451
   about 3 keV.                                                   6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
   Energy-dependence of level spacing was calculated according to 6925 1451
   the Gilbert-Cameron level density formula with associated      6925 1451
   parameters from Mughabghab [Mu06],[Mu98].                      6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
    Energy-dependence of capture widths is calculated on the      6925 1451
    basis of the generalized Fermi liquid model [Mu00] with       6925 1451
    associated parameters from [Mu06].                            6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
  Average parameters:                                             6925 1451
                S (10**4)     <D> (eV)*   <Gg> (meV)              6925 1451
    s-wave      2.22           7.28       121.9                   6925 1451
    p-wave      1.01                       61.0                   6925 1451
    d-wave      2.22                       96.5                   6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
   * Level spacing at the neutron separation energy of target+n.  6925 1451
                                                                  6925 1451
 With these parameters the 30-keV Maxwelian capture cross section 6925 1451
 is calculated as  1081-+54 mb up to  a neutron energy of 20 MeV, 6925 1451
 as compared with KADONIS's 1129-+56 mb                           6925 1451
